# ui-foundry design system

Read `design/DESIGN.md` and `design/components.md` before writing UI. Matching skills live in `.cursor/skills/`
(theme-from-inspiration, design-lint, component-build, ui-build, ui-verify) — follow the one that fits the task.

- Build screens from `{{componentsDir}}` components only; never import `@base-ui/react` in feature code.
- Style with semantic tokens only: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `rounded-lg`, `p-4`
  (CSS: `var(--color-primary)`, `var(--space-4)`). No hex/rgb/oklch, no `bg-blue-500`/`text-white`, no `p-[13px]`, no `dark:` color overrides.
- Need a new value or component? Change `design/tokens.json` → `npm run design:build`, or build the component
  (component-build skill) → `npm run design:inventory`. Never edit `design/generated/*`.
- After editing UI files run `npm run design:lint -- --files <changed files>` and fix every error.
- Before finishing UI work: dev server up → `npm run design:verify -- --routes <routes>` → view the screenshots,
  compare against DESIGN.md's Do/Don't, iterate (max 3 rounds), then report.
